ders, = Icel. ''tveir'', m., ''tvær'', f., ''tvau'', n., = Sw. ''tvenne'', ''två'' = Dan. ''tvende'', ''to'' = Goth. ''twai'', m., ''twōs'', f., ''twa'', n., = OIr. ''da'' = Lith. ''du'' = Russ. ''dva'', etc., < L. ''duo'' (> OF. ''dui'', ''dous'', ''deus'', ''deux'', F. ''deux'' = Pr. ''dui'', mod. ''dous'' = Sp. ''dos'' = Pg. ''dous'', ''dois'' = It. ''due'') = Gr. δύο = Skt. ''dva'' = Zend ''dva'', two; root unknown. The word appears as a prefix also as ''twi-'', ''twy-'', in the orig. masc. form as ''twain'', and in numerous derivatives, as ''twin''<sup>1</sup>, ''twin''<sup>2</sup>, ''twine''<sup>1</sup>, ''twine''<sup>2</sup>, ''twist'', ''twissel'', ''twizzle'', etc.] '''I.''' ''a.'' One and one; twice one: a cardinal numeral.
{{smaller block|<poem>Ech of yow, to shorte with our weye,
In this viage, shal telle tales ''tweye'', . . .
And homward he shal tellen othere ''two''.</poem>
{{right|''Chaucer'', Gen. Prol. to C. T., l. 792.}}}}
{{smaller block|<poem>A water was tham ''twa'' by-twene,
And a brig all ouer it clene.</poem>
{{right|''Holy Rood'' (E. E. T. S.), p. 125.}}}}
{{smaller|'''In two''', into two parts; asunder: as, to cut a thing ''in two''.}}
{{smaller block|<poem>At its full stretch as the tough string he drew,
Struck by an arm unseen, it burst ''in two''.</poem>
{{right|''Pope'', Iliad, xv. 545.}}}}
{{smaller|'''The two tables.''' Same as ''tables of the law'' (which see, under ''table'').—'''To be in two minds.''' See ''mind''<sup>1</sup>.}}

'''II.''' ''n.'' '''1.''' The number which consists of one and one.—'''2.''' A symbol representing this number, as 2, II, or ii.—'''3.''' A group consisting of two individuals; a duality; a pair.
{{smaller block|<poem>They were a comely ''tway''.</poem>
{{right|''Lord Livingston'' (Child’s Ballads, III. 344).}}}}
{{smaller block|Apostles who may go out in ''twos'' to academize the culture of the manufacturing districts.
{{right|''Saturday Rev.'', XXXVII. 217.}}}}
{{smaller|'''To be two''', to be at variance or irreconciled, as opposed to being ''at one''.}}

