{{right|''Hood'', Miss Kilmansegg, Her Fancy Ball.}}}}

¶
'''two-speed''' (tö′spēd), ''a.'' In ''mech.'', adapted for producing two rates of speed.—'''Two-speed pulley.''' {{smaller|See ''double-speed pulley'', under ''pulley''.}}

'''two-spotted''' (tö′spot″ed), ''a.'' Notably marked with two spots of color: specifying one of the paradoxures, ''Nandinia binotata.''

'''two-throw''' (tö′thrō), ''a.'' In ''mech.'', adapted for producing alternating throws or thrusts in two directions: as, a ''two-throw'' crank.

'''two-tongued''' (tö′tungd), ''a.'' Double-tongued; deceitful.
{{smaller block|I hate the ''two-tongued'' hypocrite.
{{right|''G. Sandys'', Paraphrase of Ps. xxvi.}}}}

'''two-toothed''' (tö′tötht), ''a.'' Having two teeth; doubly dentate; bident.

'''two-valved''' (tö′valvd), ''a.'' Bivalvular, as a shell or pod. See ''bivalve.''

'''two-way''' (tö′wā), ''a.'' '''1.''' In ''mech.'', having two
[[FIGURE]]
{{c|{{smaller|Two-way Cock.}}}}
{{c|{{smaller|''a'', position which distributes water to two branches; ''b'', ''c'', positions in which the water is passed through only one branch; ''d'', position for stopping flow.}}}}
ways or passages.—'''2.''' In ''math.'', having a double mode of variation. Thus, a surface is a ''two-way'' spread.—'''Two-way cock,''' {{smaller|a cock by which a fluid may be distributed to each of two branches or to either of them separately, or be entirely shut off.}}—'''Two-way series,''' {{smaller|a series of the form <math>A_{0,0} + A_{0,1} + A_{0,2} + \cdots + A_{1,0} + A_{1,1} + A_{1,2} + \cdots + A_{2,0} + A_{2,1} + A_{2,2} + \ldots</math> Such a series presents no intrinsic peculiarity, but is readily capable of being expressed as an ordinary infinite series.}}

